            0.126
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Grass Grasshopper Frog Snake"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.293,
            0.13,
            0.883,
            0.171
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If frogs disappear from this ecosystem, what will happen to the population of grasshoppers and snakes? Why?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.174,
            0.883,
            0.249
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. In a school garden, students noticed fewer butterflies the previous season. What could be the possible reasons? What steps can students take to have more butterflies on campus?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.254,
            0.883,
            0.293
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. Why is it not possible to have an ecosystem with only producers and no consumers or decomposers?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.294,
            0.884,
            0.35
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. Observe two different places near your home or school (e.g., a park and a roadside). List the living and non-living components you see. How are the two ecosystems different?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.351,
            0.883,
            0.407
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. ‘Human-made ecosystems like agricultural fields are necessary, but they must be made sustainable.’ Comment on the statement"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.408,
            0.883,
            0.448
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. If the Indian hare population (Fig. 12.20) drops because of a disease, how would it affect the number of other organisms?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.291,
            0.47,
            0.622,
            0.492
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Discover, design, and debate"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.036,
            0.525,
            0.259,
            0.704
          ],
          "content": [
