          "bbox": [
            0.272,
            0.506,
            0.883,
            0.582
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Plan a clean-up day at school or a nearby park. Wearing gloves and using bags, collect the litter you find. Discuss the kinds of waste you found. Which was the most common? How can we reduce such waste?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.586,
            0.884,
            0.68
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In Arunachal Pradesh, the Nyishi and Mishmi tribes treat the Tiger as sacred. In Chhattisgarh, the Baiga tribe worships the Bagesur Dev and believes the Tiger is the protector of the forest. Find out about other Indian tribes that have a special connection with animals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.684,
            0.884,
            0.779
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pick a tree near your home or school. Observe it once a week for 4 weeks. Note any new leaves, flowers, fruits, or visiting birds and insects. Record your observations. You may even upload your findings to www.seasonwatch.in and become a young citizen scientist."
            }
          ]
        },
